<title>HONG KONG: DCB Bank sets US$200 mln callable FRCDs.</title>
<headline>DCB Bank sets US$200 mln callable FRCDs.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>DCB Bank has launched a US$200 million callable floating rate certificate of deposit issue due 2002, bookrunner Merrill Lynch International said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The FRCDs can be called at interest payment dates falling two and three years after the first payment date. There are no puts.  </p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p> BORROWER DCB BANK BHD			   GUARANTOR   --</p>
<p> AMT	US$200 MLN  COUPON    6ML+22.5   MATURITY    5 YRS</p>
<p> TYPE     FRCD	  ISS PRICE PAR	  LAUNCHED    31.JAN.97</p>
<p> PUTS     NONE	  CALLS     **	   REPLIES     --</p>
<p> LISTING  NONE	  REPAYMENT BULLET     DENOMS US$500K/1MLN</p>
<p> RATINGS  NONE	  SALE LMTS STANDARD</p>
<p> NEG PLG  --	    CRS DEF   YES	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA2</p>
<p> GOV LAW  ENGLISH     HOME CTRY MALAYSIA   TAX PROV    STANDARD</p>
<p> PAY DATE 12.MAR.97</p>
<p> NOTES    CALLABLE AT INTEREST PAYMENT DATES FALLING TWO AND</p>
<p>	    THREE YEARS AFTER THE PAYMENT DATE.</p>
<p>MGT LEVELS AND FEES</p>
<p>	    SNR CO-MGRS  US$10 MLN+ 22.5 BP</p>
<p>	    C0-LEAD MGRS US$7-9 MLN 17.5 BP</p>
<p>	    CO-MANAGERS  US$3-6 MLN 12.5 BP</p>
<p>ARRANGER  MERRILL LYNCH INTERNATIONAL (BOOKS), JP MORGAN</p>
<p>	     SECURITIES, SAKURA FINANCE ASIA.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
